\subsubsection{Discarding an Active Session}

Sometimes a user wants to \emph{correct} the start time of a label that
is already being tracked---for example, after realising they forgot to
start tracking thirty minutes ago.  Simply calling [[stop_labels]]
followed by [[start_labels]] would save a spurious short entry to the
history, polluting the data.

[[discard_labels]] solves this by removing the active entry without
producing a [[TrackingEntry]].  The only structural difference from
[[stop_labels]] is the absence of the grouping-and-emit step.

Removing a label must also clean up its batch record: if the discarded
label was the sole member of its batch, the batch key is deleted.
Leaving an empty batch would let stale batch IDs accumulate and could
confuse later calls to [[stop_labels]] that look up batches by ID.

<<active session class>>=
    def discard_labels(
        self,
        labels: list[str]
    ) -> list[str]:
        """
        Remove labels from active tracking without creating entries.

        Unlike stop_labels, no TrackingEntry is produced---the in-progress
        session is silently erased.  This is used when the user wants to
        correct the start time of an active label via --replace: the old
        entry is thrown away so the label can be restarted at the desired
        time.

        Args:
            labels: Labels to discard from active tracking

        Returns:
            List of labels that were actually discarded
        """
        discarded = []
        for label in labels:
            if label not in self.active_labels:
                continue
            _, _, batch_id = self.active_labels.pop(label)
            if label in self.label_order:
                self.label_order.remove(label)
            if batch_id in self.batches:
                self.batches[batch_id] = [
                    l for l in self.batches[batch_id]
                    if l != label
                ]
                if not self.batches[batch_id]:
                    del self.batches[batch_id]
            discarded.append(label)
        return discarded

