Unsetting is best effort ([[check=False]]): a hook that cannot be
unset merely keeps wasting a [[run-shell]] per event, which is the
status quo we are improving on, not a reason to fail the launch.

<<unset superseded hook lines>>=
if is_stale is not None:
    for line in existing_lines:
        if command in line or not is_stale(line):
            continue
        match = re.match(
            rf"^{re.escape(hook_name)}\[(\d+)\]", line,
        )
        if not match:
            continue
        subprocess.run(
            [
                "tmux", "set-hook", "-u",
                "-t", target,
                f"{hook_name}[{match.group(1)}]",
