\paragraph{Migration.}
Migration rescues files that belong to \emph{this very server} but
are filed where the current code cannot find them: under an
outdated key alias, or in the persistent tracking directory.  What
makes the rescue safe is that same-server identity is provable from
the filename.  The start time in the generation comes from the
server itself, and one socket cannot host two servers at
once---so a key with the current sockethash and the current start
time but a different PID is not another server, it is this server
under its old [[$TMUX]] alias.  (A restarted server would need to
start within the same second to forge this; we accept that
coincidence, which is why the window must additionally still be
live.)  Only the label-bearing kinds are worth moving; the
last-window pointer is rewritten on the next window switch anyway,
and nothing reads the debug log.

<<constants>>=
MIGRATABLE_STATE_FILE_PREFIXES = (
    "window_labels_",
    "pane_labels_",
    "suspend_",
)
<<helper functions>>=
def migrate_tmux_state_files(
    current_server_key: str,
    dry_run: bool = False,
